 "ambiguities": [
  "4.2 partial boxes: read literally (a box not entirely inside the mesh, in x, y or z), the coarsest scale kz = 36 equals the mesh depth, so for any offset oz > 0 every depth box is partial and every event is excluded. The registration says the exclusion is 'not expected for EXP-011 central-spot events', which suggests lateral edges only. The literal rule is the default; a lateral-only rule is available as --partial-box-rule lateral_only and both fractions are always reported. Changing the applied rule is a new dated registration (researcher's decision).",
  "4.2 offsets 'drawn once': read as ONE set of 8 offsets shared by every event, drawn by rng.integers(low=(0,0,0), high=(54,54,36), size=(8,3)) from default_rng(20261109); the triples are recorded.",
  "4.3 units: the effective side is in mm (m3.EFFECTIVE_SIDE_MM); the amplitude A of b = A eps^-D_f depends on that unit, eps* does not. The fit is parameterised by (ln b at the finest scale, D_f), an exact reparameterisation of (A, D_f).",
  "4.3 'non-convergence': scipy least_squares (method lm) status <= 0, a non-finite parameter, or an exception; one deterministic start, no retry. Capacity b < 1 is clamped to 1 in the model.",
  "4.4/4.5 denominators: events excluded by 4.2 are out of every denominator; fit failures stay in and count as not admissible.",
  "6 C1-C3 use every non-excluded event on W* (the registration says ONE window for all events), including events that are not admissible on W*.",
  "5 number of disrupted blocks: exactly max(1, floor(phi * n + 0.5)) of the n occupied (layer, lateral block) units of the event (pooled over the whole event, drawn without replacement). The minimum of one is an addition so phi = 0.05 on a small event is not empty.",
  "5 variant S: 'empty' means empty in the original event; the targets are drawn without replacement. When a block has fewer empty voxels than occupied ones only as many randomly chosen occupied voxels as there are empty voxels move (the rest stay), so occupancy is still exactly preserved; the number of such blocks is reported.",
  "6 C0 applies to both statistics (D2 and D0-D2), each with its own rate; it is 'sane' only if both rates lie in 0.05 +- 3 SE (binomial SE with 200 splits), in every set.",
  "6 C2 with no testable pairing is not a pass (reported as 'not testable' and treated as matching insufficient); the registration's rule 'PASS if no Holm-adjusted p <= 0.05' would be vacuously true there.",
  "6 C2/C3 KS: the same definition as S3 stage 3 (stratified_ks_matrix, one stratum) but computed with exact integer numerators so ties in the permutation distribution are not broken by float32 rounding.",
  "6 C3: the two arms are drawn as disjoint random event subsets of the SAME set (the registration's 'independent events').",
  "4.5 when no W* exists, C1-C3 are 'reported descriptively only' on a fallback window (the >= 3-scale window with the highest minimum admissibility fraction over the sets, ties: finest then widest); that fallback is not in the registration.",
  "9 stop rule 'one event takes more than 2 s': evaluated as the maximum in-worker per-event time (mean and median also reported).",
  "8 B1 and B3 are the smooth baselines of EXP-010, not cascades: the recovery of known dimensions is computed on the S4 cascade (aligned levels of multiscale_3d) with offset averaging, which breaks the alignment of the cascade cells with the boxes; B1 and B3 are reported descriptively (ordering, fit acceptance, saturation scale).",
  "3 prefix deposit used for the C2 matching key: arrays['edep_total_mev'] (checked against the sum of the fine prefix deposits)."
 ],
